  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Kamsarmax \"Bora\" 81/2014 Sainty, China (SS 01/2029, DD 04/2027) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 22,5 mill basis waiving inspection. For reference, the sister vessel \"Sirocco\" 82/2014 Sainty, China (SS 01/2029, DD 03/2027) was sold back in May at rgn USD 20 mill. Amoysailing Maritime have committed their Panamax \"King Loong\" 77/2006 Oshima, Japan (SS 06/2031, DD 06/2029) at USD 13 mill. Remind you that the two-years-younger sister vessel \"G. B. Corrado\" 77/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 03/2028) was sold in July at USD 15 mill. Furthermore, Hanaro Shipping committed their \"Sea Orion\" 76/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS 01/2030, DD 12/2027) at USD 11,5 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Marinicki C\"76/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD 04/2028) was sold back in June at USD 11,8 mill. Chinese owners have committed the Ultramax \"Ocean Tianbao\" 63/2016 CSI, China (SS/DD 11/2026) to clients of Besiktas at USD 26,5 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Union Lotus\" 63/2015 CSI, China (SS 04/2030, DD 04/2028) was sold a month ago at USD 25,8 mill. The older \"Aeriko\" 63/2013 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 10/2028) of Prosperity Bay Shipping was committed at USD 24 mill. By way of comparison, the sister vessel \"Amaryllis\" 63/2013 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 08/2028) was committed in August at low-mid USD 24 mill. On the Supramax sector, Misuga Kaiun committed their \"Sky Knight\" 58/2012 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD 02/2028) at USD 22,5 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the one-year-older \"Stenia Colossus\" 58/2011 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 03/2031, DD 04/2029) was sold at USD 21 mill. Moreover, Atlantic Bulk Carriers committed their \"Desert Spring\" 57/2012 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 01/2027) at high USD 17 mill. For reference, same owners committed the one-year-older sister vessel \"Desert Victory\" 57/2011 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 11/2026) back in May at USD 15,4 mill. The Handysize \"Boston Harmony\" 38/2015 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 08/2030, DD 09/2028) was committed to Greek interests at high USD 23 mill. Remind you that back in July, the one-year-older \"African Harrier\" 37/2014 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2029, DD 08/2027) was sold at USD 20,1 mill.",
    "tankers": "The VLCC \"Ashoka\" 302/2010 Universal, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 03/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 130 mill, while the one-year-older \"Norns\" 310/2009 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 02/2028) was committed a week ago at USD 112 mill. In addition, Chinese owners committed the \"Xi Xiu\" 300/2003 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 01/2028) at USD 60 mill. Note that a month ago, the \"Grit\" 298/2003 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 07/2027) was sold at USD 50 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route eased slightly, with Dampier and Port Stanley departures to Qingdao settling between USD 15.95/17.20 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, maintained a firm tone between USD 41.90/43.00 fio, alongside a Seven Islands run reaching USD 46.65 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with China and Singapore-Japan options settled between USD 19,000/25,000 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan, India and South East Asia ranges fetched between USD 19,250/26,000 pd, alongside a South China trip via China to India fixing at USD 22,750 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China, Japan and India achieved between USD 14,000/23,000 pd, while a fertilizer trip from North China to India reached USD 20,000 pd. From East Coast India and West Coast India, trips via ECSA to Singapore-Japan range obtained between USD 18,750/25,000 pd, alongside an ECI coastal trip to WCI securing USD 32,500 pd. Out of South East Asia, a run via South Africa to Singapore-Japan made USD 24,000 pd. In the Atlantic, a Continent departure via NCSA to China reached USD 34,750 pd, while a West Africa trip via NCSA to Continent and Mediterranean range fetched USD 23,500 pd. On period, vessels secured between USD 17,000/22,500 pd for durations ranging from 2 laden legs up to 14 months.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, Indonesian coal trips to ECI and Thailand ranges settled between USD 22,000/23,500 pd, while steel and regional runs from North China to Singapore and ECI range obtained between USD 17,000/23,500 pd. Far East departures via PG to Mediterranean fixed between USD 22,500/25,000 pd, alongside a North China trip to USG securing USD 17,000 pd. Out of West Coast India, trips to Far East and West Africa range settled between USD 12,500/18,500 pd, while an ECI run via Indonesia back to India achieved USD 13,500 pd. From South Africa, business was active with runs to WCI, India and Far East ranges agreed between USD 21,000/26,750 pd, accompanied by ballast bonuses between USD 210,000 and USD 270,000. On period, an Ultramax fixed for 6 to 8 months duration at USD 23,500 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Atlantic, Baltic departures via ECSA options fixed at USD 22,000 pd, while a trip to Caribs range achieved USD 17,000 pd. Out of Continent, a steel run to US Gulf settled at USD 15,000 pd. From US Gulf and USEC, grain and wood pellet runs to NCSA and Continent range reached USD 22,000 pd and USD 20,000 pd respectively, while a local US Gulf trip secured USD 21,000 pd."
    }
  },
